Z||000000||GTMike||06-26-2001||05:29 AM||||ok i'm sure this question has been asked a million times. but with out nos,turbo,or engien swap.  what are some good bolt on upgrades to increas my 2.8s output.  <P>under drive pully? k&N intake?  exauset?  <P>also is there any way to reduce the weight of my care. 87 gt 5speed. with out getting rid of the AC.   maybe lighter rims and tires.  is there any thing on it that  isn't really needed that you guys take off to lose a few pounds?     i would like to be able to run a sold consistant  15s 1/4 mile     i live in colorado  at about 5,000 feet.  i know its like adding a second on to a sea level time.    i just want to be able to have a little more fun with the hondas  while i'm saveing for a 3800 sc conversion.  thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||06-26-2001||09:27 AM||||You could get: <BR>Darrel Morse bored out intake/throttle body<BR>Chris West short headers or Fiero Store Sprint manifolds<BR>MSD ignition<BR>Borla Exhaust system<BR>Underdrive pulley set<BR>Low temp fan switch and thermostat<P>Doing all of the above should get you into the mid to high 14's.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||06-26-2001||09:43 AM||||Low 15's ..I think mid to high 14's is pushing it. Since most of them run right around high 15's now with the 5spd<P><BR>Could be wrong thou. <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">      <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals. &lt;b&gt; New White Face Gauges , 75Hp Shot of NOS&lt;/b&gt;Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dave Gunsul||06-26-2001||11:58 AM||||You can port and gasket match the lower intake. It's the most restrictive part of the intake system.<BR>Darrel Morse did mine as well as the above mentioned t-body and upper plenum.<P>You can put 1.6 roller rockers on to but, despite what some people will say, you need to change the valve springs to a stiffer aftermarket (comp. cams or Crane) type or you<BR>will bind.<P>You can port the heads and switch to a bigger<BR>cam but that's probably further than you wanted to go.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000004||rc5star||06-26-2001||12:15 PM||||Im in the same boat as GTMike, just looking for a little more hp while saving up for a swap.<BR>How do you get a hold of Darrel Morse or someone else who can bore out the intake and how much does this usually cost????||||reg||5
Z||000005||GTMike||06-26-2001||03:24 PM||||porting and polising the intake and exaust manofolds are in my rangs of things to do. is there any planns or directions on the web that shows how to do it.  i did it once of my cj7 that has a 304.  but i had plans and directins guiding me threw it.   i just used a dremel tool.    <P>assuming i was at elevation.   with all the mods you named  would it run high 14s. <P>any one have any input on my weight question.<BR>thanks for all the speedy replies. <P>mike||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||06-26-2001||03:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dave Gunsul:<BR><B>You can put 1.6 roller rockers on to but, despite what some people will say, you need to change the valve springs to a stiffer aftermarket (comp. cams or Crane) type or you<BR>will bind.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Any recommendations there?||||reg||5
Z||000007||Dave Gunsul||06-26-2001||08:26 PM||||Comp. Cams high perf. springs part# 980-12<BR>Crane high perf. valve spring part# 99848-12<BR>I have a set of never opened Comp. Cams springs if anybodies interested.<BR>I'm going to be taking them to the NIFE swap meet this sunday to sell.<P>Darrel Morse's email: morse86@aol.com<BR>His prices are as follows.<BR>Bore out t-body and upper plenum = $150.00<BR>Port exhaust manifolds = $150.00<BR>Both of these prices include return shipping.<BR>He can supply the parts at an additional cost<BR>Darrel does excellent machine work, you won't be disapointed.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000008||GTMike||07-02-2001||03:27 AM||||any more info on those 1.6 rockers.  dose any one have any links to a detaild website that shows exactally what i need to do it and how to do it?    <P>how much performane gain would i see? is it expensive. is it worth the money.  <P>any one from colorado  on this board?||||reg||1
Z||000009||Dave Gunsul||07-02-2001||12:46 PM||||Price would depend on which rockers you went with. Comp. Cams sells a roller tipped rocker<BR>in either 1.52 or 1.6. These are much less expensive than a full roller rocker like the ones that Crane sells.<BR>Roller tipped rockers are usually $150.00 or more and the full roller are $280.00 or more.<P>HP gains are 15 or less for full roller 1.6<BR>rockers.<BR>Comp. Cams (magnum roller rockers) <A HREF="http://www.compcams.com" TARGET=_blank>www.compcams.com</A> <BR>Crane Cams (Gold Race rockers) <A HREF="http://www.cranecams.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cranecams.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000010||Leadfoot||07-02-2001||12:52 PM||||Check this site out.  There is some good info about performance gains for a 2.8. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.org/text/firedup.txt" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.org/text/firedup.txt</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Darekin||07-02-2001||06:05 PM||||Well so far everything I have done to my 85GT is as follows:<P>Motorvac to clean out the carbon,<BR>Higher performing ACdelco plugs,<BR>premium plug wires from Napa.<BR>K&N Air Filter (Changing to a Cold air intake system this friday)<BR>High-Flow Catalytic converter,<BR>Performance Exhaust system.<BR>We're thinking (My mechanic and myself) about putting on performance headers,<BR>depending on what the rating of my back pressure is after the intake system, and cat is put on. These are what I have done, my mechanic is telling me I am pushing close to 200hp right now if not more... Will Dyno it in a week or so to find out... Forgot about the Hypertech street runner chip, thinking about moving over to the Hypertech Thermomaster chip... keeps the engine running cooler.<P>------------------<BR>Darekin<BR>============<BR>1985 Fiero GT<BR>Performance Exhaust<BR>Hypertech Chip<BR>K&N Filter<BR>Accel Dist. coil.<BR>Hi-Flo Cat. Inst 7/6<BR>Cold Air Intake 7/6<p>[This message has been edited by Darekin (edited 07-02-2001).]||||reg||1
